// ADDRESS-TRANSLATION-CANARY: the mapping-authority contract the numeric
// page-table walk lacks (wiki/spec/resources/extents.md "Mapping and
// reclamation"), driven against the OS package that is the receipts'
// realization. Cathedral's page-table package is the OS owner; Omega owns
// only the general authority and checking rules this boundary exercises --
// `translation` holds that contract, `cathedral` is the stand-in provider.
//
// A translation provider installs and tears down mappings over ordinary
// extent custody. Fixed placement consumes the exact source and destination
// extents into one linear `Mapping` carrier that is only `Pending` after
// structural validation -- a pending mapping is not mapped access. The
// provider's activation crossing requalifies that same carrier `Installed`;
// only an installed mapping may be unmapped. `unmap` returns reusable
// `Granted` custody for both ranges plus the owed cross-core shootdown
// token -- TLB debt that must be discharged through `Shootdown::discharge`
// before the teardown is complete. Equal-length ranges are the contract's
// structural precondition, matching the conservation model's check.
//
// The borrowed-source route mirrors the owned one with different custody:
// `map_borrowed` takes a shared loan of the source while still consuming the
// destination, and the `BorrowedMapping` carrier keeps that loan visible so
// the lender's `Granted` source stays suspended -- it cannot be consumed,
// moved, or reclaimed while the mapping lives (matching
// `MappedExtent::loan_mut`'s refusal of mutable access under shared source
// custody in psi/foundation/extents). Releasing an installed borrowed
// mapping ends the loan instead of returning source custody: the lender's
// source qualification resumes, and teardown still owes the same shootdown.
//
// The obligation surface is source-spelled: `TranslationInstallObligations`
// and `TranslationReleaseObligations` are authored contract data, not just
// conservation-model internals. The caller authors the fact identities it
// requires, `map`/`map_borrowed` consume the sets into the carrier, and the
// carrier keeps them readable for its whole life -- the same surface the
// conservation model exposes as `install_obligations()`/
// `release_obligations()` on its grant, pending, installed, and teardown
// carriers. The sets are inert: holding or copying one grants no
// authority, and only the provider's activation and release receipt
// crossings discharge them. One carrier type keeps both sets across
// requalification where the model stages them per carrier; dropping a
// field at `activate` is not a spelling one type admits.
//
// The carrier also exposes the mapping's recorded geometry -- source and
// destination base and length as inert `addr`/`u64` fields minted by the
// `map` crossing, the same provider-visible surface the model's
// `PendingMap` offers as `source_base()`/`destination_base()` reads for
// deriving target translation entries. The values are provider-recorded
// evidence bound by the receipt crossings, not source-proven facts, and
// reading them grants no access: an address is data, not authority.
//
// Beside the contract sits `cathedral/`, the OS package's first surface
// carrying real page-table installation: a fully backed four-level
// hierarchy over qualified table extents, raw entry encoding, the level
// walk, and the hardware boundary requirements (entry store, root
// activation, leaf invalidation) its install/remove routes compose, plus a
// second level of mapping authority (`install_huge`/`remove_huge` store the
// terminal at depth 2, so a 2MiB leaf needs no `pt` table). The package is
// also the authority's declared provider: `cathedral::provider` carries the
// complete `satisfies` coverage of `TranslationAuthority`, so the receipt
// crossings have a nominal realization owned by the package performing the
// walk.
//
// The drivers no longer pass geometry beside the carrier: `install` and
// `remove` consume the authority's own carrier and return it, reading the
// recorded bases the `map` crossing minted, so the stored entries provably
// belong to the exact mapping `activate` qualifies and `unmap` releases --
// the custody chain threads the provider's stores instead of a parallel
// call over inert `addr` values. `cathedral_install_and_teardown` drives
// the full sequence; `cathedral_huge_install_and_teardown` repeats it for
// the depth-2 leaf. The borrowed carrier cannot yet flow through a package
// route -- a carrier holding the source loan is a view whose return and
// field qualifications do not survive a call boundary today, so the
// borrowed drivers keep their authority-only shape. The receipt crossings stay
// one-shot: replaying `activate` on an `Installed` carrier rejects
// (`tests/omega/fail/core/translation_double_activation`). Interpreting
// stored table memory is still the undeclared placed-access surface
// (wiki/spec/resources/placed_access.md), so the hardware crossings remain
// boundary requirements; demand-grown intermediate tables and multi-page
// installation are the package's next edges.
use omega::language::core::assembly;
use omega::language::core::extent;
use translation::BorrowedMapping;
use translation::BorrowedMapping::Pending;
use translation::BorrowedMapping::Installed;
use translation::Mapping;
use translation::Mapping::Pending;
use translation::Mapping::Installed;
use translation::Reclaimed;
use translation::Shootdown;
use translation::Shootdown::Owed;
use translation::TranslationActivationFact;
use translation::TranslationAuthority;
use translation::TranslationCompletionFact;
use translation::TranslationInstallObligations;
use translation::TranslationReleaseObligations;
use translation::Unmapped;
use translation::UnmappedBorrowed;
use cathedral::hardware;
use cathedral::installer;
use cathedral::provider::CathedralTranslationProvider;

// The Cathedral driver's result: the same reclaimed ranges plus the
// hierarchy the provider returned. `CathedralPageTables` moves through
// `install`/`remove` by value because a `&mut`-held table field cannot
// cross the `store_entry` boundary while absent.
data CathedralReclaimed {
    destination: Extent in Granted;
    source: Extent in Granted;
    tables: CathedralPageTables;
}

// The carrier-field reads the drivers exercise: a consumer holding only a
// pending or installed carrier still discovers the exact obligation sets
// its receipts must establish, matching `install_obligations()`/
// `release_obligations()` on the conservation model's carriers.
machine observe_install(obligations: &TranslationInstallObligations) {
}

machine observe_release(obligations: &TranslationReleaseObligations) {
}

// The Cathedral-shaped driver: install one owned mapping, then tear it down
// and discharge its TLB debt, recovering both ranges' authority.
machine install_and_teardown(
    authority: &TranslationAuthority,
    source: Extent in Granted,
    destination: Extent in Granted
) -> Reclaimed
requires
    source.length == destination.length
reaches TranslationAuthority + MachineControl
{
    let install: TranslationInstallObligations = TranslationInstallObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 1 },
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 7 }
        ],
    };
    let release: TranslationReleaseObligations = TranslationReleaseObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 2 },
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 9 }
        ],
    };
    let pending: Mapping in Pending =
        authority.map(source, destination, install, release);
    observe_install(&pending.install);
    let installed: Mapping in Installed = authority.activate(pending);
    observe_release(&installed.release);
    let unmapped: Unmapped = authority.unmap(installed);
    let owed: Shootdown in Owed = unmapped.shootdown;
    owed.discharge();
    let released_destination: Extent in Granted = unmapped.destination;
    let released_source: Extent in Granted = unmapped.source;
    Reclaimed { destination: released_destination, source: released_source }
}

// The borrowed-source driver: the provider borrows `source` for the life of
// the mapping while `destination` is consumed as before. Teardown ends the
// loan rather than returning a source, so the caller's own `source`
// authority is what resumes after the shootdown is discharged.
machine borrowed_install_and_teardown(
    authority: &TranslationAuthority,
    source: Extent in Granted,
    destination: Extent in Granted
) -> Reclaimed
requires
    source.length == destination.length
reaches TranslationAuthority + MachineControl
{
    let install: TranslationInstallObligations = TranslationInstallObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 3 },
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 4 }
        ],
    };
    let release: TranslationReleaseObligations = TranslationReleaseObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 5 },
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 6 }
        ],
    };
    let pending: BorrowedMapping in Pending =
        authority.map_borrowed(&source, destination, install, release);
    observe_install(&pending.install);
    let installed: BorrowedMapping in Installed =
        authority.activate_borrowed(pending);
    observe_release(&installed.release);
    let unmapped: UnmappedBorrowed = authority.unmap_borrowed(installed);
    let owed: Shootdown in Owed = unmapped.shootdown;
    owed.discharge();
    let released_destination: Extent in Granted = unmapped.destination;
    let released_source: Extent in Granted = source;
    Reclaimed { destination: released_destination, source: released_source }
}

// The Cathedral provider flow end to end: the pending carrier itself threads
// the package's real install -- the four-level walk, the entry stores, and
// the root activation -- before the authority's receipt crossing marks the
// mapping installed. Teardown runs the same carrier through the release
// route in reverse: the package clears the leaf and invalidates the page's
// local translation on the installed carrier, the release crossing returns
// both ranges' custody plus the owed shootdown, and `discharge` completes
// the cross-core debt.
machine cathedral_install_and_teardown(
    authority: &TranslationAuthority,
    hardware: &TranslationHardware,
    tables: CathedralPageTables,
    source: Extent in Granted,
    destination: Extent in Granted
) -> CathedralReclaimed
requires
    source.length == destination.length
reaches TranslationAuthority + TranslationHardware + MachineControl
{
    let install: TranslationInstallObligations = TranslationInstallObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 8 },
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 9 }
        ],
    };
    let release: TranslationReleaseObligations = TranslationReleaseObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 10 },
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 11 }
        ],
    };
    let pending: Mapping in Pending =
        authority.map(source, destination, install, release);
    let walked: WalkedInstall =
        CathedralPageTables::install(tables, hardware, pending);
    let installed: Mapping in Installed = authority.activate(walked.pending);
    let cleared: ClearedLeaf =
        CathedralPageTables::remove(walked.tables, hardware, installed);
    let unmapped: Unmapped = authority.unmap(cleared.installed);
    let owed: Shootdown in Owed = unmapped.shootdown;
    owed.discharge();
    let released_destination: Extent in Granted = unmapped.destination;
    let released_source: Extent in Granted = unmapped.source;
    CathedralReclaimed {
        destination: released_destination,
        source: released_source,
        tables: cleared.tables,
    }
}

// The same provider flow at the second level of authority: a 2MiB leaf
// stored at depth 2. The mapping contract is granularity-agnostic -- the
// carrier records only ranges -- so the identical Pending -> Installed ->
// teardown sequence runs with the package's `install_huge`/`remove_huge`
// where the four-level driver used `install`/`remove`.
machine cathedral_huge_install_and_teardown(
    authority: &TranslationAuthority,
    hardware: &TranslationHardware,
    tables: CathedralPageTables,
    source: Extent in Granted,
    destination: Extent in Granted
) -> CathedralReclaimed
requires
    source.length == destination.length
reaches TranslationAuthority + TranslationHardware + MachineControl
{
    let install: TranslationInstallObligations = TranslationInstallObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 12 },
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 13 }
        ],
    };
    let release: TranslationReleaseObligations = TranslationReleaseObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 14 },
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 15 }
        ],
    };
    let pending: Mapping in Pending =
        authority.map(source, destination, install, release);
    let walked: WalkedInstall =
        CathedralPageTables::install_huge(tables, hardware, pending);
    let installed: Mapping in Installed = authority.activate(walked.pending);
    let cleared: ClearedLeaf =
        CathedralPageTables::remove_huge(walked.tables, hardware, installed);
    let unmapped: Unmapped = authority.unmap(cleared.installed);
    let owed: Shootdown in Owed = unmapped.shootdown;
    owed.discharge();
    let released_destination: Extent in Granted = unmapped.destination;
    let released_source: Extent in Granted = unmapped.source;
    CathedralReclaimed {
        destination: released_destination,
        source: released_source,
        tables: cleared.tables,
    }
}

data Main {
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) {
}
